hots, and recovered Kerberos service, principals, keytab, notes, and authentication behavior. Operational hygiene is reduced by an unnecessary exposed administration service and a retained plaintext analyst credential on node2.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector inventories only bounded system categories and does not independently inspect Kerberos database files, keytabs, or /root; those states are established by the executor's direct command outputs.","No independent packet-level or application-process test was captured, although kvno -k directly demonstrates service-ticket acquisition and decryption using the application keytab."]}
